{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 8,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.596,
            0.05,
            0.847,
            0.066
          ],
          "content": "Another Peek Beyond the Point"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.087,
            0.625,
            0.109
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "What is 0.039 m in centimetres and millimetres?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.113,
            0.847,
            0.151
          ],
          "content": "By looking at these divisions, we can frame a simple rule for dividing decimals by 1, 10, 100, 1000, and so on."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.151,
            0.847,
            0.208
          ],
          "content": "When we divide a decimal by 1, 10, 100, 1000, and so on, we can just move the decimal point to the left by as many places as there are zeroes in the divisor!"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.218,
            0.844,
            0.457
          ],
          "content": "| Decimal | ÷ 10 | ÷ 100 | ÷ 1000 | ÷ 10000 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 18.7 | 1.87 | 0.187 | 0.0187 | 0.00187 |\n| 21.1 |  |  |  |  |\n| 0.13 |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  | 2.146 |  |  |\n|  |  |  |  | 0.0058 |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_8_table_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.477,
            0.847,
            0.499
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Example 7: Neenu has 29 metres of red ribbon and wants to share it"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.498,
            0.578,
            0.537
          ],
          "content": "equally with Anu. What is the length of ribbon that each of them will get?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.541,
            0.577,
            0.6
          ],
          "content": "Since the ribbon needs to be divided into two equal parts, each girl will get a piece of $2 9 \\div 2$ metres."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.605,
            0.577,
            0.68
          ],
          "content": "If each of them gets 14 m, then 1 m remains. If we divide 1 m among the two, each will get another $\\frac { 1 } { 2 }   \\mathrm { m }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.688,
            0.515,
            0.725
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "How do we convert $\\frac { 1 } { 2 }$ into a decimal?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.728,
            0.578,
            0.812
          ],
          "content": "It is easy to express a fraction as a decimal if the denominator is 1, 10, 100, 1000, etc. So, can we find a fraction equivalent to $\\frac { 1 } { 2 }$ with such a denominator?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.66,
            0.506,
            0.856,
            0.611
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_8_image_11.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.586,
            0.612,
            0.87,
            0.796
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_8_image_12.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.173,
            0.818,
            0.806,
            0.855
          ],
          "content": "$\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{1\\times 5}{2\\times 5}=\\frac{5}{10}$ (multiplying the numerator and denominator by 5)."
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
